        <mxCell id="steps_box" parent="1" style="fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;spacing=8;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fillColor=#F7F9FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;spacing=12;fontColor=#333333;" value="&lt;b&gt;ONBOARDING&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&#39;font-size:10px&#39; color=&#39;#777777&#39;&gt;(distributor, one-time setup in AdminOps)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;① Register one ERP connection per instance — erp_type, base_url, credentials.&lt;br&gt;② Register the subsidiary and point it at that connection plus the Odoo company id. One connection belongs to one subsidiary.&lt;br&gt;③ Bind each reseller who buys from that instance, recording that instance&#39;s own erp_customer_id. Two instances means two bindings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEN, ON EACH POLL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;④ Sales writes the quotation in that ERP. The worker reads sale.order for each verified binding and keeps the order only when company_id matches the subsidiary.&lt;br&gt;⑤ Confirm, delivery, and invoice update the same order. AdminOps shows the order and every notification sent to the reseller. A later purchase order uses the same route and the same customer id, in the other direction." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="770" width="1180" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
